{"kind": "mod", "id": 2150, "name": "No Save On Death - Respawned", "slug": "no-save-on-death-respawned", "teaser": "A keep your equipment style mod that still punishes you for death.", "owner_name": "takenmake", "downloads": 4568, "favourites": 1, "featured": false, "contains_ads": false, "contains_ai_content": false, "cheat_notice": false, "license_name": "MIT License", "guid": "com.takenmake.nosaveondeath", "thumbnail_local": null, "category": "Items", "category_id": 4, "updated_at": "2026-07-28T07:24:50.000000Z", "created_at": "2025-05-24T23:30:25.000000Z", "published_at": "2026-03-11T10:59:00.000000Z", "latest_constraint": "~4.0 <4.1.0", "latest_version": "2.0.0", "has_local": false, "has_github": false, "license_link": "https://choosealicense.com/licenses/mit/", "description_html": "<p>This is a mod based on toaddsworth’s <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1557-nosaveondeath/?highlight=nosave\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">NoSaveOnDeath</a> mod. Earlier versions of the mod were more of an update, however with the release of SPT 4.0 the mod had to be completely rewritten and so only the general concept remains the same at this point. Here’s a short snippet of the original description to explain what the mod does:</p>\n<p>“<em>This mod makes it so that when you die in raid, your progress is not saved. This means that in the event that you die, go MIA, or quit the raid through the menu, everything including gear, experience, and quest progress is restored to how it was before you went on the raid.</em>”</p>\n", "versions": [{"version": "1.1.1", "spt_version_constraint": "~3.11.0", "content_length": null, "downloads": 2049, "published_at": "2026-06-21T21:31:00.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/2150/no-save-on-death-respawned/1.1.1", "github_url": null, "external_url": null, "local_path": null, "fika_compatibility": "unknown", "dependencies": []}, {"version": "2.0.0", "spt_version_